Xray Forge talks to, and can launch, third-party proxy cores (Xray-core,
sing-box, mihomo, sing-box-extended, Psiphon's ConsoleClient). Those programs
are not part of this work and keep their own licenses; they are neither bundled
nor relicensed by it.

Installers and executables also contain third-party libraries (Python and its
standard library, curl_cffi, PyYAML, cryptography, PyInstaller's runtime,
Electron and Chromium, and the npm packages listed in electron/package-lock.json).
Each keeps its own license and notices.
